From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve explicit build-host Go garbage-collection tuning

Blueprint launches soong_build with env -i. Preserve GOGC when the build
owner explicitly supplies it, so a bounded compiler does not reclaim its
working heap through swap. This controls the host compiler only; Android
product configuration and generated module rules are unchanged.

Upstream: Android Soong, Apache-2.0, retained pinned LineageOS 20 source.

diff --git a/ui/build/soong.go b/ui/build/soong.go
--- a/ui/build/soong.go
+++ b/ui/build/soong.go
@@ -167,6 +167,9 @@ func primaryBuilderInvocation(
 
 	commonArgs = append(commonArgs, "-l", filepath.Join(config.FileListDir(), "Android.bp.list"))
 	invocationEnv := make(map[string]string)
+	if gc := os.Getenv("GOGC"); gc != "" {
+		invocationEnv["GOGC"] = gc
+	}
 	debugMode := os.Getenv("SOONG_DELVE") != ""
 
 	if debugMode {
